  "findings": [
    "Interface shape alone does not encode stream order or repeated reads; converters require local buffering, and subsequent buffer folding has stricter matching requirements.",
    "Tiling/fusion and resource allocation interact. HLS/vendor profiling supplies latency, initial delay and initiation interval; it is not a universal hardware-perfect cost model.",
    "FIFO sizing uses cumulative produced and consumed tokens; conservative equalization may trade latency for buffering. A pairwise occupancy result is not a general whole-graph deadlock proof.",
    "On-board U55C/Vitis 2024.1 evaluation runs one fused Transformer block repeatedly with different weights. GPU/FPGA formats differ; no speed ratio adopted."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The prose references Algorithm 1 lines 17–19 and Algorithm 2 lines beyond the displayed listings; do not claim line-by-line implementation verification.",
    "Dynamic shape support uses upper-bound hints; runtime-value-dependent control flow can fall back to host PyTorch.",
    "Published GPU comparison does not establish current vLLM/SGLang optimality or identical quality/quantization; no general FPGA-vs-GPU recommendation.",
    "Support for additional spatial platforms is future work; no V4/K3 production support or new GPU feature inferred."
  ],
